declarations.documentation:
Parse JSON text directly as a T — `parse` then `validate[T]`, the typed text boundary. Instantiate T
explicitly (it appears only in the result, so it cannot be inferred). Malformed text throws `parse_error`;
a value that does not conform to T's schema throws `validation_error` naming the offending path.

A subscription's whole memory, in one value — the thing `resume` writes to the store, so it is also
the thing an operator reads in the console when a subscription looks stuck. Internal to `subscribe`;
an app never builds one.

